* TMUX1308A behavioral single-channel cell (one of 8 S pins -> common D pin)
*
* Pins : s  = source pin (S0..S7)
*        d  = common drain pin (D)
*        c  = analog enable, 0 V = off, 1 V = on (generated by the netlist from
*             the address/timing schedule, so ton/toff/edge are configurable)
*
* Global .param values used (all set by build_model.py from config.json):
*   mux_ron, mux_ron_vdep, mux_vref, mux_roff, mux_cs_off, mux_c_on_extra, mux_c_ft,
*   mux_qinj, mux_qinj_src_frac, mux_ileak_s_off
*
* Effects modelled:
*   - on resistance (with a quadratic signal dependence), off isolation
*   - off-state source capacitance, extra capacitance while selected (the datasheet
*     on-capacitance is a single lumped value, so the extra is CON - CSOFF - CDOFF),
*     source-to-drain feedthrough capacitance (from off isolation / crosstalk specs)
*   - charge injection: net charge mux_qinj is delivered when the channel turns
*     off (and removed when it turns on), split between D and S
*   - off-state source->drain leakage (mux_ileak_s_off)
*   Drain-side capacitance and on-state drain leakage are shared by all
*   channels and live in the top-level netlist.
.subckt TMUX_CH s d c
Bsw s d I=V(s,d)*(limit(V(c),0,1)/({mux_ron}*(1+{mux_ron_vdep}*(V(s)-{mux_vref})*(V(s)-{mux_vref}))) + (1-limit(V(c),0,1))/{mux_roff})
Cso s 0 {mux_cs_off}
Cft s d {mux_c_ft}
Con s x {mux_c_on_extra}
Rx  x 0 1G
Bgx x 0 I=V(x)*limit(V(c),0,1)/{mux_ron}
Bqd 0 d I=-{mux_qinj}*(1-{mux_qinj_src_frac})*ddt(limit(V(c),0,1))
Bqs 0 s I=-{mux_qinj}*{mux_qinj_src_frac}*ddt(limit(V(c),0,1))
Bls s d I={mux_ileak_s_off}*(1-limit(V(c),0,1))
.ends TMUX_CH
